# Evidence artifacts are BYTE-LEVEL records, not source code: never let git
# normalise their line endings.
#
# Why: docs/evidence/**/windows/*.txt are produced on Windows and are CRLF in
# their original form. With core.autocrlf=input (this repo), committing them
# would rewrite CRLF -> LF inside the object store, so a fresh clone would no
# longer hold the bytes the instrument actually wrote -- and any later
# hash-based verification of the archive would silently disagree with the
# original. This is the same hazard as TRAPS 60 ("a bare MD5 across platforms
# compares line endings, not content"); here the normaliser would have done it
# for us without asking.
docs/evidence/** -text
